          "type": "study",
          "settings": {
            "stat": "2,409–4,964",
            "stat_label": "Microplastics a year, estimated",
            "title": "Plastic cookware can add microplastics to home-cooked food",
            "text": "<p>Researchers estimated that cooking with plastic kitchen items, including utensils, boards and nonstick pans, could add roughly 2,400 to 5,000 microplastic particles a year to home-cooked food. Cookware without plastic added none.</p><p>It's a modelled estimate based on one home-cooked meal a day.</p>",
