            "title": "Nylon utensils can release plastic compounds into hot food",
            "text": "<p>Germany's Federal Institute for Risk Assessment (BfR) tested 33 nylon (polyamide) kitchen utensils. In lab tests, 10 released more plastic oligomers than its 5 mg per kg of food guideline.</p><p>Its advice: keep nylon utensils' contact with hot food, above 70 °C, as brief as possible.</p>",
